  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3003.01 Persons Qualified for A Hardship Registration",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3003.01 Persons Qualified for A Hardship Registration. In order to qualify for a hardship registration, a person shall have been:\n\n(a) Certified as a habitual offender;\n\n(b) Convicted of negligent homicide involving the use of a motor vehicle;\n\n(c) Convicted of manslaughter involving the use of a motor vehicle;\n\n(d) Convicted of a subsequent offense of driving under the influence of intoxicating liquor or any controlled drug pursuant to RSA 265-A:2; or\n\n(e) Convicted of aggravated driving while intoxicated pursuant to RSA 265-A:3.\n\nSource. #5027, eff 12-19-90; ss by #6296, eff 7-23-96, EXPIRED: 7-23-04\n\nNew. #8181, eff 9-25-04; ss by #10085, eff 1-31-12; ss by #13279, eff 10-19-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3000.html"
